{"title":"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle is inscribed in trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/b/a6b7be80a447e3064828d457331a37443b73829e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PS = QR = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" /> cm, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/469bf920f9b3e02183cc2479d01ceb49cdca9645.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> cm and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/c/b0c4431d9bf53ce1862e5c1dfdd1c6897a1bb91a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SR = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> cm, what is the length of the diameter of the circle?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa9b17ec5388f83e5cb18b6a1211e4fc2a4d4aed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 14 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 25 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 24 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\sqrt{544} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\sqrt{674}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"426\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can notice that the diameter of the circle is just the height of the diameter from the diagram. We can draw the heights of and name the points that they meet the trapezoid at. This will also form two right triangles and a rectangle.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd7db9202db08b7c54a81c8afecf617b8a479fd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, the height of the trapezoid be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/7/ff70857c4d09e25f7542cc00ab34118701e3002e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YR = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>However, we notice that the right triangles must be congruent because the hypotenuses are the same and one of the legs is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> in both triangles. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/397fd7b1f33bdbf6ee27a83d1bcee42d222cb331.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. This means that we can replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> in the diagram.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b5b6984adef8b774125db659de459778772b61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" /> because it is part of the rectangle. Thus, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e97c740891d6b2bcca27ed6755e79310e1d7d732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SX + XY + YR = a + 18 + a = SR = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"333\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/2/d222ddcebab18e6578f62101c2ed32c45fb73545.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a + 18 = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/7/da75e7d40eaf8d69a3b8d73d51eeb909bf9648db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a = 32 - 18 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/e/0eee938e33ce487889f3e1d126721706fc5e7690.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 14 \\div 2 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" /> cm\n</p><p>We can now focus on one of the right triangles, as both are equal.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Using this right triangle, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/5/6e517d9bd2516ffd9994ed150e88b1752a3a9137.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^{2} + 7^{2} = 25^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/3/ee361611a35d4c0a40b60b5af88cccbd759ba56e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h^{2} = 25^{2} - 7^{2} = 625 - 49 = 576$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"252\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cfdf2be67e8e5c1cfc6487f8944d1e3e492c46f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 25 (page does not exist)\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_